<title>USA: Union Carbide Corp Q3 earnings summary.</title>
<headline>Union Carbide Corp Q3 earnings summary.</headline>
<dateline>DANBURY, Conn. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary     $1.19		    $1.96</p>
<p> Shr diluted     1.08		     1.77</p>
<p> Net		 161,000		  277,000</p>
<p> Net sales	 1,538,000		1,495,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary133,436		  140,324</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted149,781		  156,874</p>
<p>	  NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary     $3.52		    $5.11</p>
<p> Shr diluted     3.20		     4.61</p>
<p> Net		 491,000		  735,000</p>
<p> Net sales	 4,598,000		4,489,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary136,875		  142,086</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted153,167		  159,223</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call mean estimate for Q3 was $1.10 a share.</p>
<p>The 1995 third quarter results include a gain of $161 million, or $0.32 per share, from the sale of its remaining interests in UCAR International Inc, and a $68 million charge for postemployment benefits, including severance.</p>
<p>Figures for the first nine months of 1995 include a $381 million gain from the sale of its remaining interests in UCAR International Inc, and a $191 million charge for future lease payments on unused office space primarily at the company's Danbury headquarters.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
